  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1144 AM CDT Fri Jul 17 2026\n\nInto the work week, temperatures will only continue to increase as \nWAA increases at 850mb. This will lead to triple digit heat indices \ninto early next week, some getting into Heat advisory territory. We \nwill have to evaluate the need for a heat product as we continue to \napproach that point in time. Remember to stay hydrated and take \nfrequent breaks in the AC or shade if you work outside or have any \nactivities planned. Until the cold front comes through on Wednesday \nbringing cooler and less humid air into Middle Tennessee, diurnal \nthunderstorms will continue to be a daily threat. Most of these will \nnot be strong, but we could see some gusty winds and localized flash \nflooding from stronger or training storms. \n\nAfter the cold front on Wednesday morning, we will enter a quieter \nperiod for the mid-week. Highs will be in the mid 80s for Thursday \nand Friday, slowly warming back into the 90s into next weekend.",
